Subject: identities may be made as Ed25519
Why: Quiver's simulation of its persisted class (kiln's CP-T2.2 step 6, AC-T2.2.5) replays a run from its seed: an ECDSA P-256 certificate verify is a DER document whose length is as random as its nonce, so a handshake's flight was a byte longer or shorter from one run to the next, and a tenth of the seeds ran apart across processes; Ed25519's are 64 bytes every time. The default stays ECDSA P-256

